{"case_id":"C008","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","configuration","input_semantics","attack_surface"],"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["decoder.decode_image_config?","decoder.do_decode_image_config?","decoder.decode_frame_config?","decoder.do_decode_frame_config?","decoder.decode_frame?","decoder.do_decode_frame?","decoder.from_src_to_pixels?","decoder.from_pixels_to_dst!","decoder.restart_frame!"],"reason":"H0 exclusively enables and exercises the JSON modules through wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson. It neither enables a HANDSUM module nor constructs or calls the new Handsum decoder, so S1's image-decoding entry points and state machine receive no fuzz coverage. This misses fuzz-worthy 48-byte Handsum header/version/aspect-ratio semantics, streaming and closed-input behavior, frame decoding into caller-selected pixel buffers and blend modes, and restart/call-sequence transitions.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__AUX__JSON, with no Handsum module definition.","H0's fuzz_complex and fuzz_simple only call wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens; fuzz_cpp only calls wuffs_aux::DecodeJson.","S1 adds pub struct decoder? implements base.image_decoder with call_sequence, swizzler, dimensions, and internal pixel buffers.","decoder.do_decode_image_config? parses the '\\xFE\\xD7' little-endian signature, version bits c32 & 0xC0, orientation bit c32 & 0x20, and aspect-ratio bits c32 & 0x1F.","decoder.decode_image_config?, decoder.decode_frame_config?, and decoder.decode_frame? translate a closed-input $short read into #truncated input.","decoder.do_decode_frame? calls pixel_swizzler.prepare! using args.dst.pixel_format(), args.dst.palette(), and args.blend, then decoder.from_pixels_to_dst! writes rows derived from width and destination bits_per_pixel.","decoder.restart_frame! and decoder.do_decode_frame_config? implement observable transitions through call_sequence values 0x20, 0x28, 0x40, and 0x60 and validate io_position 3."],"recommended_action":"Add a Handsum image-decoder fuzz harness that enables the Handsum and required base modules, feeds arbitrary and segmented/closed inputs through decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, and decode_frame?, varies destination pixel formats, palettes, blend modes, and buffer layouts, and exercises valid and invalid restart_frame! and call-order sequences while checking statuses, bounds, progress, and memory safety."}
